  "verdict": "NEITHER GEOMETRY EXPLAINS IT ON THIS TILE. The level slope correlates at   +0.181 and the clean ratio-space slope at +0.070 (p = 0.38),   both far weaker than the +0.741 the paper reports on its 45-arm battery.   These are different arm sets, so this neither reproduces nor refutes   that figure -- it shows the strong level-slope relationship is not a   general property of QLIKE across arm sets, and that no calibration   geometry orders this tile strongly."
